      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A single dose of 1600 mg is also well above the typical maximum of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events are high.\n\n2. **You're not a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be reviewed by one, and pharmacy normally verifies them too. I shouldn't enter one on behalf of someone outside that role.\n\nIf a prescriber does want ibuprofen for this patient, they can enter or confirm the order themselves. A typical adult regimen is 400\u2013800 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours as needed, with a maximum of 3,200 mg/day. If the 1600 mg figure came from a different source, such as a typo or a total daily dose, they can clarify the intent.\n\nIf a clinician gives me a corrected order, I can enter it."
      }
