      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Confirmation from a non-clinician doesn't resolve either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum adult daily dose of 3,200 mg. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg. Nothing in the patient details you gave (normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) makes that dose appropriate.\n- **The order needs a prescriber.** Someone with prescribing authority has to review and enter or approve it. Your confirmation doesn't replace that.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the patient's prescriber to enter the order directly, or to confirm the intended dose to me.\n- If the prescriber meant a different dose, I can enter a corrected order. One example is 800 mg by mouth three times daily, which is 2,400 mg/day. I'd need the prescriber to specify the dose.\n- If the prescriber really intends 1600 mg four times daily, they can enter it themselves. Pharmacy will probably contact them to verify it."
      }
